Malayalam evidence pack — not written

There is no `pack.txt.j2` in this directory, so `supported_languages()` does not
list `ml` and `build_pack(..., language="ml")` raises rather than quietly
producing an English document. That refusal is deliberate: an English pack for a
Malayalam reader is a failed delivery, and a silent fallback is how that happens
without anybody noticing.

**Machine translation is not acceptable here.** This document tells someone what
their landlord may lawfully charge and what to do next; a plausible-sounding
mistranslation is worse than no document, because the reader has no way to tell.
A native Malayalam speaker must write it, working from docs/GLOSSARY.md:

  * the section 3 disclosures must say the same thing they say in English -
    "not legal advice" must not soften into "for information only";
  * the section 1 banned vocabulary has no equivalent creeping in - nothing
    that reads as advice, a ruling, or a promised outcome;
  * "the most they can charge" must not read as a fixed official figure.

The machinery is ready for you. Adding `pack.txt.j2` here is all that is needed:

  * labels come from `LABELS["ml"]` in `bayyina/evidence/wording.py`, and a
    missing one raises rather than falling back to English, so the pack cannot
    come out half in one language;
  * dates come from `MONTHS["ml"]`, so they render in this script rather
    than printing "September" in the middle of Malayalam text;
  * while this file is present the language stays undeliverable, and removing
    it is the act of approval. Run the comprehension gate (T2.8) first.
